{"title": "Sectional Mock #74 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>If (a + b + c) = 12, and (ab + bc + ca) = 47, find the value of (a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (a + b + c) = 12 &#2324;&#2352; (ab + bc + ca) = 47 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup> - 3abc &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["24", "36", "48", "42"], "options_hi": ["24", "36", "48", "42"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><b>We know that:</b> (a + b + c)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2(ab + bc + ca)</p><p>12<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2 * 47</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = 144  -  94 = 50</p><p>Now, </p><p>(a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc) = (a + b + c) [(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>)  -  (ab + bc + ca)]</p><p>= 12 * [50  -  47]</p><p>= 12 * 3</p><p>= 36</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>We know that:</b> (a + b + c)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2(ab + bc + ca)</p><p>12<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2 * 47</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> = 144  -  94 = 50</p><p>Now, </p><p>(a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc) = (a + b + c) [(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>)  -  (ab + bc + ca)]</p><p>= 12 * [50  -  47]</p><p>= 12 * 3</p><p>= 36</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the speeds of a boat upstream and downstream is 2:3, and the sum of these two speeds is 15 km/h. What is the speed of the stream?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2:3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 15 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3.5 km/h", "1.5 km/h", "3 km/h", "2.5 km/h"], "options_hi": ["3.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "1.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "3 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "2.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Upstream = b - s, Downstream = b + s</p><p>2b = 15, b = 7.5</p><p>(7.5 - s)/(7.5 + s) = 2/3</p><p>3(7.5 - s) = 2(7.5 + s)</p><p>22.5 - 3s = 15 + 2s</p><p>s = 1.5 km/h</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Upstream = b - s, Downstream = b + s</p><p>2b = 15, b = 7.5</p><p>(7.5 - s)/(7.5 + s) = 2/3</p><p>3(7.5 - s) = 2(7.5 + s)</p><p>22.5 - 3s = 15 + 2s</p><p>s = 1.5 km/h</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify the following expression:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">91<sup>0</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup> - 3<sup>3</sup> - 2<sup>4</sup>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">91<sup>0</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup> - 3<sup>3</sup> - 2<sup>4</sup>", "options_en": ["0", "1", "-26", "-32"], "options_hi": ["0", "1", "-26", "-32"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=116 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image010.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=55 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=41 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image013.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=116 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image010.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=55 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=41 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23007/image013.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>The perimeter of one face of a cube is 72 cm. Find the total surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of cube.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 72 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2426", "1872", "1944", "2004"], "options_hi": ["2426", "1872", "1944", "2004"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Perimeter of one face = 72 cm</p><p>Side length of cube = 72/4 = 18 cm</p><p>Total surface area = 6 * side * side</p><p>= 6 * 18 * 18</p><p>= 1944 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Perimeter of one face = 72 cm</p><p>Side length of cube = 72/4 = 18 cm</p><p>Total surface area = 6 * side * side</p><p>= 6 * 18 * 18</p><p>= 1944 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of [(243<sup>n/5</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>)/(9<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>n  -  1</sup>)]?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>[(243<sup>n/5</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>)/(9<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>n - 1</sup>)] &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["9", "12", "6", "15"], "options_hi": ["9", "12", "6", "15"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>= [(243<sup>n/5</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>)/(9<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>n  -  1</sup>)]</p><p>= [{(3<sup>5</sup>)<sup>n/5</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>}/{(3<sup>2</sup>)<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>n  -  1</sup>}]</p><p>= [(3<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>)/(3<sup>2n</sup> * 3<sup>n  -  1</sup>)]</p><p>= (3<sup>(n + 2n + 1)</sup>)/(3<sup>(2n + n  -  1)</sup>)</p><p>= 3<sup>(3n + 1)</sup>)/(3<sup>(3n  -  1)</sup>)</p><p>= 3<sup>(3n + 1  -  3n + 1)</sup></p><p>= 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 9</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>= [(243<sup>n/5</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>)/(9<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>n  -  1</sup>)]</p><p>= [{(3<sup>5</sup>)<sup>n/5</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>}/{(3<sup>2</sup>)<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>n  -  1</sup>}]</p><p>= [(3<sup>n</sup> * 3<sup>2n + 1</sup>)/(3<sup>2n</sup> * 3<sup>n  -  1</sup>)]</p><p>= (3<sup>(n + 2n + 1)</sup>)/(3<sup>(2n + n  -  1)</sup>)</p><p>= 3<sup>(3n + 1)</sup>)/(3<sup>(3n  -  1)</sup>)</p><p>= 3<sup>(3n + 1  -  3n + 1)</sup></p><p>= 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 9</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ashutosh bought a table of &#8377;12425 and made a down payment of some amount. He paid the remaining amount in two equal instalments of &#8377;6171 at 10% rate of compound interest. Find the down payment made by Ashutosh.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2358;&#2369;&#2340;&#2379;&#2359; &#2344;&#2375; &#8377;12425 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2375;&#2348;&#2354; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#8377;6171 &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 10% &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2310;&#2358;&#2369;&#2340;&#2379;&#2359; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;1828", "&#8377;1960", "&#8377;1680", "&#8377;1715"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;1828", "&#8377;1960", "&#8377;1680", "&#8377;1715"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let down payment = d</p><p><img width=232 height=63 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21860/image004.png\"></p><p>12425  -  d = 5610 + 5100</p><p>d = 12425 - 10710</p><p>d = &#8377;1715</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let down payment = d</p><p><img width=232 height=63 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21860/image004.png\"></p><p>12425  -  d = 5610 + 5100</p><p>d = 12425 - 10710</p><p>d = &#8377;1715</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A farm has some turkeys and sheep. If the total number of heads is 50 and the total number of legs is 134, how many turkeys are there on the farm?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2335;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2349;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2367;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 50 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 134 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2335;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["31", "29", "33", "32"], "options_hi": ["31", "29", "33", "32"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let number of turkeys be X then number of sheep are (50  -  X).</p><p>Total number of legs = 134</p><p>2X + 4(50  -  X) = 134</p><p>2X + 200  -  4X = 134</p><p>2X = 66</p><p>X = 33</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let number of turkeys be X then number of sheep are (50  -  X).</p><p>Total number of legs = 134</p><p>2X + 4(50  -  X) = 134</p><p>2X + 200  -  4X = 134</p><p>2X = 66</p><p>X = 33</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the remainder 529 x 147 x 79 is divided by 15.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>529 x 147 x 79 &#2325;&#2379; 15 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4", "12", "9", "6"], "options_hi": ["4", "12", "9", "6"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "\"<p><span><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/8abbb93b4c0b11b06fa3d41ee6c831b7.png\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p><span><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/8abbb93b4c0b11b06fa3d41ee6c831b7.png\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If X(sin<sup>2</sup> 57&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup> 33&deg;) + 4(cosec<sup>2</sup> 61&deg; - tan<sup>2</sup> 29&deg;) + cos<sup>2</sup> 45&deg; =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">X", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X(sin<sup>2</sup> 57&deg; - cos<sup>2</sup> 33&deg;) + 4(cosec<sup>2</sup> 61&deg; - tan<sup>2</sup> 29&deg;) + cos<sup>2</sup> 45&deg; = <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">X", "options_en": ["27/2", "23/2", "25/2", "29/2"], "options_hi": ["27/2", "23/2", "25/2", "29/2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=395 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=448 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=343 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=49 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=395 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=448 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=343 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=49 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18553/image006.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the figure above, AB is parallel to PQ and angles are as shown in the figure. What is &#8736;AOP equal to:</p><p><img width=189 height=97 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image001.png\" ></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AB, PQ &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#8736;AOP &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"189\" height=\"97\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image001.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["62&deg;", "126&deg;", "32&deg;", "94&deg;"], "options_hi": ["62&deg;", "126&deg;", "32&deg;", "94&deg;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=186 height=101 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image002.png\" ></p><p>Draw a line KL from O</p><p>&#8736;AOL = &#8736;BAO = 63&deg; [Alternate angle]</p><p>&#8736;POL = &#8736;QPO = 31&deg; [alternate angle]</p><p>Hence, &#8736;AOP = 63&deg; + 31&deg; = 94&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=186 height=101 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24663/image002.png\" ></p><p>Draw a line KL from O</p><p>&#8736;AOL = &#8736;BAO = 63&deg; [Alternate angle]</p><p>&#8736;POL = &#8736;QPO = 31&deg; [alternate angle]</p><p>Hence, &#8736;AOP = 63&deg; + 31&deg; = 94&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum increased by 20% at some rate of simple interest in T years. The compound interest on Rs.12000 at same rate of interest in 3 years is Rs. 3972 when compounded annually. What should come in place of T?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; T &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 12000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; 3972 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; T &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2310;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["4 years", "3 years", "1 year", "2 years"], "options_hi": ["4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "1 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let, the rate of interest be R%.</p><p>Then, CI = 12000  X  ((1+R/100)<sup>3 </sup> - 1) = 3972</p><p>(1+R/100)<sup>3</sup> = (3972+12000)/12000</p><p>(100+R)<sup>3</sup> = 1331000</p><p>R = 10%</p><p>Now, at simple rate of interest,</p><p>20% of sum = sum X  10 X  T/100</p><p>T = 2 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, the rate of interest be R%.</p><p>Then, CI = 12000  X  ((1+R/100)<sup>3 </sup> - 1) = 3972</p><p>(1+R/100)<sup>3</sup> = (3972+12000)/12000</p><p>(100+R)<sup>3</sup> = 1331000</p><p>R = 10%</p><p>Now, at simple rate of interest,</p><p>20% of sum = sum X  10 X  T/100</p><p>T = 2 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of (cos<sup>2</sup>40&deg; + cos<sup>2</sup>50&deg;)/(sec<sup>2</sup>30&deg; - 1)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(cos<sup>2</sup>40&deg; + cos<sup>2</sup>50&deg;)/(sec<sup>2</sup>30&deg; - 1) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1", "1/3", "&radic;3", "3"], "options_hi": ["1", "1/3", "&radic;3", "3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>(cos<sup>2</sup>40&deg; + cos<sup>2</sup>50&deg;)/(sec<sup>2</sup>30&deg; - 1)</p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>40&deg; + sin<sup>2</sup>40&deg;)/(tan<sup>2</sup>30&deg;)</p><p>= 1/(1/3)</p><p>= 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(cos<sup>2</sup>40&deg; + cos<sup>2</sup>50&deg;)/(sec<sup>2</sup>30&deg; - 1)</p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>40&deg; + sin<sup>2</sup>40&deg;)/(tan<sup>2</sup>30&deg;)</p><p>= 1/(1/3)</p><p>= 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the given rectangle, if &#8736; CFO = 55&deg;, and &#8736; COD = 102&deg;, then find the value of &#8736; OCD.</p><p><img width=239 height=125 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image006.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736; CFO = 55&deg;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#8736; COD = 102&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736; OCD &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=239 height=125 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image006.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["37&deg;", "43&deg;", "42&deg;", "48&deg;"], "options_hi": ["37&deg;", "43&deg;", "42&deg;", "48&deg;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=239 height=125 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image007.png\"></p><p>CF || DE</p><p>So, &#8736; CFO = &#8736; EDO = 55&deg; [alternate angles]</p><p>Therefore, &#8736; ODC = 90  -  55 = 35&deg;</p><p>Now, in &#916; COD,</p><p>&#8736; OCD = 180  -  (&#8736; ODC + &#8736; COD)</p><p>= 180  -  (35 + 102)</p><p>= 180  -  137</p><p>= 43&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=239 height=125 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image007.png\"></p><p>CF || DE</p><p>So, &#8736; CFO = &#8736; EDO = 55&deg; [alternate angles]</p><p>Therefore, &#8736; ODC = 90  -  55 = 35&deg;</p><p>Now, in &#916; COD,</p><p>&#8736; OCD = 180  -  (&#8736; ODC + &#8736; COD)</p><p>= 180  -  (35 + 102)</p><p>= 180  -  137</p><p>= 43&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of :</p><p><img width=453 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9857/image007.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p><img width=\"453\" height=\"37\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9857/image007.png\"></p><p>&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; :</p>", "options_en": ["59.375", "55.225", "47.325", "51.275"], "options_hi": ["59.375", "55.225", "47.325", "51.275"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>We know, a<sup>2</sup>  -  b<sup>2</sup> = (a + b)(a  -  b)</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2 </sup>= a<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + b<sup>2</sup></p><p>And, a<sup>3</sup>  -  b<sup>3</sup> = (a  -  b)(a<sup>2 </sup>+ ab + b<sup>2</sup>), then</p><p><img width=483 height=171 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9857/image008.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know, a<sup>2</sup>  -  b<sup>2</sup> = (a + b)(a  -  b)</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2 </sup>= a<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + b<sup>2</sup></p><p>And, a<sup>3</sup>  -  b<sup>3</sup> = (a  -  b)(a<sup>2 </sup>+ ab + b<sup>2</sup>), then</p><p><img width=483 height=171 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9857/image008.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two trains of length 360 m and 540 m respectively, at the same time both trains started moving towards each other in opposite directions on parallel tracks and crossed each other in 18 seconds. If the speed of a larger train is 20 m/sec, then find the speed of a smaller train. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 360 m &#2324;&#2352; 540 m &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2346;&#2335;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 20 m/sec &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2350; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10 m/s", "15 m/s", "25 m/s", "30 m/s"], "options_hi": ["10 m/s", "15 m/s", "25 m/s", "30 m/s"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the speed of the smaller train be 'a' m/s. </p><p>Time = Distance/ Speed</p><p>18 seconds = (360 + 540)/ (20 + a) [when running in the opposite direction, add speed]</p><p>20 + a = 900/ 18</p><p>20 + a = 50</p><p>a = 50  -  20 </p><p>a = 30 m/s</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the speed of the smaller train be 'a' m/s. </p><p>Time = Distance/ Speed</p><p>18 seconds = (360 + 540)/ (20 + a) [when running in the opposite direction, add speed]</p><p>20 + a = 900/ 18</p><p>20 + a = 50</p><p>a = 50  -  20 </p><p>a = 30 m/s</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the profit percentage of a person on an article if the ratio of cost price and selling price of the article is 9 : 15(Approx.). </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9: 15 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340;(&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["48", "54", "25", "67"], "options_hi": ["48", "54", "25", "67"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price and selling price of the article be 9x and 15x respectively</p><p>According to question,</p><p>Profit% = (S.P.  -  C.P.)/C.P. * 100</p><p>= (15x  -  9x)/9x * 100 </p><p>= 6x/9x * 100 = 66.66666 &#8773; 67%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price and selling price of the article be 9x and 15x respectively</p><p>According to question,</p><p>Profit% = (S.P.  -  C.P.)/C.P. * 100</p><p>= (15x  -  9x)/9x * 100 </p><p>= 6x/9x * 100 = 66.66666 &#8773; 67%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two vessels contain a mixture of liquid A and liquid B. In the first vessel, the ratio of liquids A to B is 3: 2; in the second, the ratio is 3: 1. A 24-liter cask is filled from these vessels to contain a mixture of liquids A and B in 2: 1. Find the amount taken from the first vessel.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357; A &#2360;&#2375; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:2 &#2361;&#2376;; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:1 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2368;&#2346;&#2366; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; 2:1 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["50/3 L", "20/3 L", "10 L", "40/3 L"], "options_hi": ["50/3 L", "20/3 L", "10 L", "40/3 L"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Using Alligation method,</p><p>Ratio of mixing = [(3/4) - (2/3)]/[(2/3) - (3/5)]</p><p>= (1/12)/(1/15)</p><p>= 5/4</p><p>Amount taken from the first vessel = 24 x 5/9 = 40/3 L</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Using Alligation method,</p><p>Ratio of mixing = [(3/4) - (2/3)]/[(2/3) - (3/5)]</p><p>= (1/12)/(1/15)</p><p>= 5/4</p><p>Amount taken from the first vessel = 24 x 5/9 = 40/3 L</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many natural numbers less than 1000 are both perfect squares and perfect cubes?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1000 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2328;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["4", "5", "3", "2"], "options_hi": ["4", "5", "3", "2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>There are only 3 number less than 1000 which are both perfect squares and perfect cubes = 1, 64, 729</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>There are only 3 number less than 1000 which are both perfect squares and perfect cubes = 1, 64, 729</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Below bar graph shows the number of employees who present and absent in five months (April, May, June, July, and August):</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22821/image007.png\"></p><p>The number of absent employees in May and August together is what percentage more or less than the number of absent employees in April, June and July together? (correct to one decimal)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; (&#2309;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2354;, &#2350;&#2312;, &#2332;&#2370;&#2344;, &#2332;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2327;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22821/image007.png\"></p><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2327;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2309;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2354;, &#2332;&#2370;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366;&#2312; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2340;&#2325;)</p>", "options_en": ["6.16%", "8.75%", "5.13%", "10.09%"], "options_hi": ["6.16%", "8.75%", "5.13%", "10.09%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The number of absent employees in May and August together = 44 + 30 = 74</p><p>The number of absent employees in April, June, and July together = 24 + 18 + 36 = 78</p><p>So, required percentage = (78  -  74)/ 78 * 100 = 5.13%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The number of absent employees in May and August together = 44 + 30 = 74</p><p>The number of absent employees in April, June, and July together = 24 + 18 + 36 = 78</p><p>So, required percentage = (78  -  74)/ 78 * 100 = 5.13%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the circumference of base of the cylinder is 132 cm and its height is 36 cm then what will be the approximate volume of the cylinder?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 132 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["0.05 m<sup>3</sup>", "0.01 m<sup>3</sup>", "0.07 m<sup>3</sup>", "0.1 m<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["0.05 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "0.01 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "0.07 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "0.1 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let's assume that the base radius of the cylinder = R cm</p><p>According to the question; 2&#960;R = 132</p><p>=&gt; 2  X  22/7  X R=132</p><p>=&gt; R = (132  X  7)/(22  X  2)= 21 cm</p><p>Now volume of the cylinder = &#960; R<sup>2</sup>h = 22/7  X  21  X  21  X  36</p><p>= 49896cm<sup>3</sup> = 0.05 m<sup>3</sup> (Approx)</p><p>(1cm = 0.01 m = 10<sup>-2</sup> m, hence 1 cm<sup>3 </sup>= 10<sup>-6 </sup>m<sup>3</sup>)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let's assume that the base radius of the cylinder = R cm</p><p>According to the question; 2&#960;R = 132</p><p>=&gt; 2  X  22/7  X R=132</p><p>=&gt; R = (132  X  7)/(22  X  2)= 21 cm</p><p>Now volume of the cylinder = &#960; R<sup>2</sup>h = 22/7  X  21  X  21  X  36</p><p>= 49896cm<sup>3</sup> = 0.05 m<sup>3</sup> (Approx)</p><p>(1cm = 0.01 m = 10<sup>-2</sup> m, hence 1 cm<sup>3 </sup>= 10<sup>-6 </sup>m<sup>3</sup>)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x + y + z = 3, xy + yz + zx = -4 and xyz = -4, then (x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup>) is equal to ______ .</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x + y + z = 3, xy + yz + zx = -4 &#2324;&#2352; xyz = -4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup>) &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["60", "62", "51", "58"], "options_hi": ["60", "62", "51", "58"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = (x + y + z)<sup>2</sup>  -  2(xy + yz + zx)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = (3)<sup>2</sup>  -  2(-4)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = 9 + 8</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = 17</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = (x + y + z)(x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup>  -  xy  -  yz  -  zx) + 3xyz</p><p>x<sup>3 </sup>+ y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 3[17  -  (-4)] + 3(-4)</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 63  -  12</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 51</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = (x + y + z)<sup>2</sup>  -  2(xy + yz + zx)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = (3)<sup>2</sup>  -  2(-4)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = 9 + 8</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = 17</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = (x + y + z)(x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup>  -  xy  -  yz  -  zx) + 3xyz</p><p>x<sup>3 </sup>+ y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 3[17  -  (-4)] + 3(-4)</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 63  -  12</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup> + z<sup>3</sup> = 51</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If x&radic;5 +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x&radic;5 + <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["62", "78", "66", "45"], "options_hi": ["62", "78", "66", "45"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>x&radic;5 + 1/x&radic;5 + 3 = 11</p><p>x&radic;5 + 1/x&radic;5 = 11  -  3 = 8</p><p>(x&radic;5 + 1/x&radic;5)<sup>2</sup> = 64</p><p>5x<sup>2</sup> + 1/5x<sup>2</sup> + 2 = 64</p><p>5x<sup>2</sup> + 1/5x<sup>2</sup> = 64  -  2</p><p>5x<sup>2</sup> + 1/5x<sup>2</sup> = 62</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x&radic;5 + 1/x&radic;5 + 3 = 11</p><p>x&radic;5 + 1/x&radic;5 = 11  -  3 = 8</p><p>(x&radic;5 + 1/x&radic;5)<sup>2</sup> = 64</p><p>5x<sup>2</sup> + 1/5x<sup>2</sup> + 2 = 64</p><p>5x<sup>2</sup> + 1/5x<sup>2</sup> = 64  -  2</p><p>5x<sup>2</sup> + 1/5x<sup>2</sup> = 62</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum of three digits of a number is 18. The digit in hundreds place is twice the digit in tens place and the digit in tens place is 2/3 <sup>rd</sup> of the digit in ones place. Find the product of the digits of the number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 18 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2376;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2342;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2342;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; 2/3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["242", "171", "216", "192"], "options_hi": ["242", "171", "216", "192"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let, the digit in ones place = m</p><p>Digit in tens place = 2m/3</p><p>Digit in hundreds place = 2 * 2m/3 = 4m/3</p><p>m + 2m/3 + 4m/3 = 18</p><p>=> 9m/3 = 18</p><p>=> m = 6</p><p>Hence, the number = 846</p><p>Product of the digits of the number = 8*4*6 = 192</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, the digit in ones place = m</p><p>Digit in tens place = 2m/3</p><p>Digit in hundreds place = 2 * 2m/3 = 4m/3</p><p>m + 2m/3 + 4m/3 = 18</p><p>=> 9m/3 = 18</p><p>=> m = 6</p><p>Hence, the number = 846</p><p>Product of the digits of the number = 8*4*6 = 192</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;A student was asked to find the simplified value of 2&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; 2 <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["16(19/20)", "8(9/40)", "14(9/20)", "6(19/40)"], "options_hi": ["16(19/20)", "8(9/40)", "14(9/20)", "6(19/40)"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>By BODMAS rule: <img width=284 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image133.png\"></p><p>= <img width=243 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image139.png\"></p><p>= <img width=212 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image140.png\"></p><p>= <img width=173 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image141.png\"></p><p>= <img width=111 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image142.png\"></p><p>= <img width=49 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image143.png\"></p><p>= <img width=24 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image144.png\"></p><p>= <img width=33 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image145.png\"></p><p>Sum of his answer and correct answer = <img width=25 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image134.png\"></p><p>So, his answer = <img width=145 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image146.png\"></p><p>Hence, absolute difference = <img width=156 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image147.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>By BODMAS rule: <img width=284 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image133.png\"></p><p>= <img width=243 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image139.png\"></p><p>= <img width=212 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image140.png\"></p><p>= <img width=173 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image141.png\"></p><p>= <img width=111 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image142.png\"></p><p>= <img width=49 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image143.png\"></p><p>= <img width=24 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image144.png\"></p><p>= <img width=33 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image145.png\"></p><p>Sum of his answer and correct answer = <img width=25 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image134.png\"></p><p>So, his answer = <img width=145 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image146.png\"></p><p>Hence, absolute difference = <img width=156 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8499/image147.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>The length and breadth of a rectangle are A cm and B cm respectively. If A: B = 17: 14 and A  -  B = 18, then find the perimeter of rectangle.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; A cm &#2324;&#2352; B cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A: B = 17: 14 &#2324;&#2352; A - B = 18 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["392 cm", "366 cm", "344 cm", "372 cm"], "options_hi": ["392 cm", "366 cm", "344 cm", "372 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let A = 17X and B = 14X</p><p>Given,</p><p>A  -  B = 18</p><p>3X = 18</p><p>X = 6</p><p>So, A = 102 cm, B = 84 cm</p><p>Perimeter of rectangle = 2 * (A + B) = 2 * (102 + 84) = 372 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let A = 17X and B = 14X</p><p>Given,</p><p>A  -  B = 18</p><p>3X = 18</p><p>X = 6</p><p>So, A = 102 cm, B = 84 cm</p><p>Perimeter of rectangle = 2 * (A + B) = 2 * (102 + 84) = 372 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}]}